:1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Fund transaction fees (charged to the AP)**\n\n- **Fixed fee:** Covers standard processing costs per creation or redemption order, such as transfer-agent and custodian settlement and transfer costs. It is charged per order, regardless of size.\n- **Variable fee:** Covers trade-dependent costs, such as brokerage commissions, spreads, market impact and taxes. These arise when the fund trades securities, e.g., for cash creations, cash substitutions or custom baskets.\n\n**Who bears them:** The authorized participant pays, typically passing the fees to its customer. This protects existing shareholders from dilution, consistent with Rule 6c-11.\n\n**Recipients may differ:** The variable fee usually goes to the fund to offset trading costs. The fixed fee may go to the custodian, transfer agent, or adviser (if it pays those costs).\n\n**AP compensation is separate:** APs earn arbitrage profits and may charge clients commissions or markups. These are not fund charges and are not paid to or by the fund.","ttft_ms":1347,"type":"result","duration_ms":3828,"uuid":"2d3d52fe-9994-42da-8e07-da398aef7363","ttft_stream_ms":1089,"time_to_request_ms":57,"first_content_frame_ms":1089,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
